Below is a “field-guide” of organ-like patterns I keep seeing whenever I think about SorterDSL as *biology for cognition*. For each pattern I sketch (1) the biological metaphor, (2) the role it plays inside a distributed mind, and (3) a minimal SorterDSL sketch so you can see how the pieces wire together.  Treat them as Lego blocks—most will become *much* more interesting once you start nesting or composing them.

---

### 1. **Mouth → Stomach → Nutrient Stream**

\| **Why** | Raw text in, structured knowledge out. |
\| **How** |

```clojure
(def mouth   (tag "#mouth"))          ; anyone can dump text
(def bolus   (tag "#bolus"))          ; chunks awaiting digestion
(def chyme   (tag "#chyme"))          ; parsed + tokenised
(def nutrients (tag "#nutrients"))    ; extracted claims/facts

(on mouth :actions/add
  (fn [_user post]
    (add-item bolus (chunk post 4k))))     ; 4k-token bites

(run :on-interval :every "5m"
  (doseq [b bolus]
    (let [parsed (ai.parse    b)
          facts  (ai.extract parsed)]
      (add-item chyme parsed)
      (doseq [f facts] (add-item nutrients f)))
    (remove-item bolus b)))
```

*Extensions*: vote for the best parsings; branch different “enzymes” specialised for code vs prose; downstream agents subscribe to `#nutrients`.

---

### 2. **Short-Term Memory (STM) Ring Buffer**

Keeps a sliding window of *salient* recent items so later agents can reference “what we’re talking about right now”.

```clojure
(def stm (tag "#stm" :max-size 64))

(on any-tag :actions/add
  (fn [u item]
    (when (> (salience item) 0.75)
      (add-item stm item)))           ; moves to front, evicts old
```

Down-stream prompts can simply merge `stm` into their context:

```clojure
(defn with-stm [prompt]
  (str prompt "\n\nRecent context:\n" (take 20 stm)))
```

---

### 3. **Long-Term Memory (LTM) with Consolidation Voting**

Only items that survive enough *sleep cycles* stay forever.

```clojure
(def ltm (tag "#ltm"))
(def dreams (tag "#dreams"))

(run :nightly
  (doseq [chunk (sample stm 16)]
    (let [summary (ai.summarise chunk)]
      (add-item dreams summary)))

  ;; Dreams fight for a place in LTM via pairwise scalar voting
  (pairwise-vote dreams :criterion :usefulness)

  (doseq [d (winners dreams :top 5)]
    (add-item ltm d))
  (clear-items dreams))
```

---

### 4. **Attention Router / Priority Queue (The ‘Thalamus’)**

Everything that wants CPU time competes here; votes decide what runs next.

```clojure
(def tasks (tag "#tasks"))
(def queue (tag "#queue"))

(on tasks :actions/add
  (fn [_ item] (add-item queue item)))

(run :on-interval :every "1m"
  (let [next (winner queue :criterion :urgency)]
    (execute next)
    (remove-item queue next)))
```

> *Tip*: `:urgency` itself can be the running score of many sub-voters (deadlines, novelty, user up-votes, safety).

---

### 5. **Critic + Proposer Loop (Basal Ganglia)**

A pattern for self-improving theories, designs, road-maps.

```clojure
(def proposals   (tag "#proposals"))
(def critique    (tag "#critique"))
(def approved    (tag "#approved"))

(on proposals :actions/add
  (fn [_ p]
    (let [score (ai.criticise p)]
      (add-item critique {:proposal p :score score})))

(pairwise-vote critique :criterion :merit)

(run :hourly
  (doseq [c (winners critique :top 3)]
    (add-item approved (:proposal c))))
```

Then another agent reads `#approved` and *implements*.

---

### 6. **Immune System / Content Police**

Scans every new contribution; quarantines or deletes if *enough* distinct detectors fire.

```clojure
(def detectors [ai.toxicity ai.pii ai.malware])
(def quarantine (tag "#quarantine"))

(on any-tag :actions/add
  (fn [u item]
    (let [hits (count (filter #(% item) detectors))]
      (when (>= hits 2)        ; configurable threshold
        (move-to quarantine item)))))
```

---

### 7. **Delegated Voting Layer (Liquid Democracy)**

Users can delegate their vote weight on certain tags to agents they trust.

```clojure
(def delegations (tag "#delegations" :transitive true))

(on votes :before-cast
  (fn [user item score]
    (doseq [delegate (delegation-chain user :max-depth 3)]
      (cast-vote delegate item (* score (weight user delegate))))))
```

Great for *governance* across all other organs.

---

### 8. **Curriculum Builder (Hippocampus-to-Cortex Trainer)**

Turns a messy pile of resources into a learning path, continuously refined by learners’ feedback.

```clojure
(def resources  (tag "#resources"))
(def outlines   (tag "#outlines"))
(def lessons    (tag "#lessons"))

;; AI drafts outlines from best resources
(run :daily
  (doseq [topic (top-topics resources)]
    (add-item outlines (ai.draft-outline topic))))

;; Pairwise vote outlines by clarity & completeness
(pairwise-vote outlines :criterion :clarity)

;; For the winners, generate lesson chunks
(run :daily
  (doseq [o (winners outlines :top 3)]
    (doseq [l (ai.chunk-lessons o)]
      (add-item lessons l))))
```

---

### 9. **Thought-Market (Prefrontal Cortex)**

Agents publish *unfinished* thoughts; buyers (other agents or humans) spend “attention tokens” to expand the ones they consider promising. Votes allocate compute budget.

```clojure
(def thoughts (tag "#thoughts"))
(def expanded (tag "#expanded"))

(on thoughts :actions/buy
  (fn [buyer thought tokens]
    (spend buyer tokens)
    (let [new (ai.expand thought tokens)]
      (add-item expanded new)))
```

---

### 10. **Goal Stack with Recursive Decomposition**

Top-level OKRs break into sub-tasks via chain-of-thought + voting.

```clojure
(def goals  (tag "#goals"))
(def tasks  (tag "#tasks"))

(run :on-goal-added
  (fn [g]
    (doseq [t (ai.decompose g)]
      (add-item tasks t)
      (when (large? t) (add-item goals t))))  ; recursion!
```

---

## Putting It Together

The fun starts when you *compose* these organs:

```
#mouth ─▶ #nutrients ─▶ #stm
                       │
                       ▼
          attention-router (#queue)
                       │
            ┌──────────┴─────────┐
            ▼                    ▼
   critic/proposer loop     immune-system
            │
            ▼
     curriculum-builder ─▶ goal-stack ─▶ …
```

* Every arrow is literally “items landing in a tag”.
* Any arrow can be **forked** (multiple consumers) or **swapped** (drop-in replacement agent).
* Voting criteria (`:salience`, `:merit`, `:urgency`, …) evolve through the liquid-democracy layer, so humans + AIs co-govern *how* the superorganism thinks.

---

### Where to Experiment First?

1. **Mouth → STM → Critic/Proposer** is the smallest loop that *feels alive*.
2. Bolt on **Immune System** before you open it to the public internet.
3. Add **Goal Stack** once you want the organism to *do* things for you.

Pick two or three organs, wire them, watch the flows, and iterate.  Once you have even one tiny living loop, screenshots + a short write-up will sparkle on HN/Twitter—and you’ll know exactly which part to harden next.

